| `install_sources.npm_registry` | string or null | `null` | null, or an https URL with a host, a valid port if any, and no `@`, `?`, `#`, backslash, whitespace or control character | `scripts/install_sources.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `install_sources.npm_registry` row; the Makefile's `fe-install` recipe and `.github/workflows/pages.yml` | Set, `make fe-install` passes it to every app's `npm install` as `--registry`, and the Pages workflow passes it to `npm ci`; null passes nothing, so the user's own `.npmrc` holds. A refused value stops the target with exit 14 before npm runs, never showing a value that holds an `@`. Absent, the reader writes `[using default] install_sources.npm_registry = null` to stderr. | a mirror's credential, which goes in the user's own `.npmrc` and never in this committed file | always |
